      "writtenOn": "2020-11-16T02:51:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It just occurred to me that we should make sure that KM will never attest to this key. The obvious way to meet the KM tag-handling requirements is to selectively place enforced tags in hw-enforced and put everything else in sw-enforced. It\u0027s actually a requirement that KM not strip sw-enforced tags it doesn\u0027t know. The reason for this is so that we can add new features and implement SW-enforcement in keystore when the KM is old and doesn\u0027t understand it.\n\nAnyway, the point is that this flow will make it easy for KM implementations to treat Tag::IDENTITY_CREDENTIAL_KEY as an unknown tag and drop it in the SW-enforced list. Although IAs should be looking for it in the hw-enforced list, they could be fooled if they\u0027re not paying attention to which list they found it in.\n\nTo prevent this we can (1) have a KeyMint VTS test that checks/specifies the correct behavior (which in this case is either to return an error or just silently strip it) and (2) have keystore filter it out of any incoming requests -- or return an error.  I\u0027m not sure which makes more sense, filter or error (in case KM is old). It\u0027d be nice if we could write a CTS test to validate (2), but I don\u0027t see a way to do that.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 357,
        "startChar": 42,
        "endLine": 357,
        "endChar": 65
      },
      "revId": "e12f631f0cf57c99e207a5a4e5f7d7a75eb20d9d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
